    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="1008" n="888" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg888"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2451: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-09T17:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1922—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 10—9:12
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>To Stevens. My January 10, 6 p.m.<anchor n="64" xml:id="d698-f1"/> Wang Nai-pin
                    has refused to take office as president [<hi rendition="#italic">director
                        general</hi>] of the Chinese Eastern <pb facs="1009" n="889" xml:id="pg889"
                    /> Railway. Because of fear that the power of the Technical Board will be
                    broadened no other Chinese of the old school is willing to accept the position,
                    so Dr. C. C. Wang has been appointed as acting head of the railway.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
